## AI-Assisted

## Instance-parent directories for pam_namespace polyinstantiation
## (/etc/security/namespace.d/30_security-misc.conf).
##
## pam_namespace requires each instance_prefix parent to pre-exist, owned
## root:root, mode 0000 (the restrictive mode is the isolation guarantee; a
## laxer mode would let one account reach another's instance).
##
## /tmp and /dev/shm instances live on the dedicated hardened tmpfs
## /run/security-misc (run-security\x2dmisc.mount); it is a fresh tmpfs at every
## boot, so these two parents are recreated here each boot (the mount unit is
## ordered before systemd-tmpfiles-setup). /var/tmp is on-disk and persistent:
## Debian ships 'q /var/tmp 1777 root root 30d', whose age cleanup would wipe
## the instances and eventually rmdir the parent (denying login, as the module
## is required), so the 'x' line excludes that subtree from age cleanup.
##
## man tmpfiles.d
d /run/security-misc/tmp-inst  0000 root root -
d /run/security-misc/shm-inst  0000 root root -
d /var/tmp/tmp-inst            0000 root root -
x /var/tmp/tmp-inst
